{"id":"caesar","name":"Caesar","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:caesar"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Caesar","text":"The title assumed by the Roman emperors after Julius Caesar. In the New Testament this title is given to various emperors as sovereigns of Judaea without their accompanying distinctive proper names (John 19:15; Acts 17:7). The Jews paid tribute to Caesar (Matt. 22:17), and all Roman citizens had the right of appeal to him (Acts 25:11). The Caesars referred to in the New Testament are Augustus (Luke 2:1), Tiberius (3:1; 20:22), Claudius (Acts 11:28), and Nero (Acts 25:8; Phil. 4:22)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"G2541","lemma":"Καῖσαρ","xlit":"Kaîsar","gloss":"Cæsar, a title of the Roman emperor","kjv":"Cæsar","count":5,"share":1},{"strong":"G3625","lemma":"οἰκουμένη","xlit":"oikouménē","gloss":"land","kjv":"earth, world","count":2,"share":0.4}],"verses":["Luke.2.1","Luke.3.1","Luke.20.22","Acts.11.28","Phil.4.22"],"related":[{"id":"roman-empire","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.04,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"appeal","type":"lexical","strong":"G2541","why":"both lead with Καῖσαρ (G2541)"},{"id":"augustus","type":"lexical","strong":"G2541","why":"both lead with Καῖσαρ (G2541)"},{"id":"citizens","type":"lexical","strong":"G2541","why":"both lead with Καῖσαρ (G2541)"},{"id":"roman-empire","type":"lexical","strong":"G2541","why":"both lead with Καῖσαρ (G2541)"}],"works":[{"work":"wars","title":"The Wars of the Jews","count":234,"chapters":[{"chapter":"WarI.20","count":19,"book":"War 1","title":""},{"chapter":"WarI.10","count":16,"book":"War 1","title":""},{"chapter":"WarII.2","count":10,"book":"War 2","title":""},{"chapter":"WarI.23","count":9,"book":"War 1","title":""},{"chapter":"WarI.33","count":9,"book":"War 1","title":""}]},{"work":"philo","title":"The Works of Philo Judaeus","count":26,"chapters":[{"chapter":"PhiloIV.4","count":14,"book":"Philo IV","title":"ON THE VIRTUES AND ON THE